# No hardcodes, brief path

Do not invent string/number literals for things the project already names. Reach the target with the shortest existing API.

- Keys, routes, storage, versions, env, log levels → enums (`AppStorageKeys`, `LoggerLevel`, `AppPages`, …).
- User-visible copy → `Texts.to.*`. Branding / const version → `AppInfo` / `AppDeveloperInfo`.
- Timeouts, paddings, filenames → `AppDefaults`, `AppPaddings`, `AppTexts`.
- Reuse extensions and existing services instead of a new helper that only wraps one call.
- Skip extra variables, wrappers, and comments that do not change behavior.

```dart
// ❌ BAD
await storage.write('appData', data);
LoggerService.to.info(message: 'Storage Cleared Successfully'); // new copy, new key

// ✅ GOOD
await storage.write(AppStorageKeys.appData.name, data);
LoggerService.to.info(message: Texts.to.storage.exceptionSaveData);
```
